confconsole (2.2.3+keel3) trixie; urgency=low

  * Usage screen: centre the mark above it. It was prepended as it was read,
    so it sat against the left edge of the dialog; the whole block is now
    shifted by one indent, measured from its widest line, on the same width
    the mark is admitted on.
  * keelbanner: take the mark's size from the installed files instead of
    stating it, so the overlay can redraw the art without a change here.

 -- Keel Linux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 18:00:06 +0000

confconsole (2.2.3+keel2) trixie; urgency=low

  * Add the Instance menu: view the instance description, apply it, show the
    drift between it and the machine, and export what the machine says as a
    description. The menu is a front end over the keel client (keelcli), so
    the console and the command line answer from the same code.
  * Usage screen: put the mark above it, dropping to the small mark and then
    to none before the addresses lose a line, so a serial console and an
    80x24 terminal both render it.
  * Recommend keel rather than suggest it: the Instance menu calls it, and
    without it the menu says so instead of failing, so it stays a
    recommendation and the package remains installable on its own.

 -- Keel Linux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:03:04 +0000

confconsole (2.2.3+keel1) trixie; urgency=low

  * ifutil: add the static IPv6 writer, NetworkInterfaces.set_static6 and
    set_dhcp6 with the module wrappers set_static6, set_dhcp6 and get_ip6conf;
    get_ipv6conf prefers a stable address over a temporary one.
  * Networking menu: add the Static IPv6 entry (address/prefix, gateway,
    name server), clearing every field restores inet6 dhcp.
  * Usage screen: show IPv6 first, on the screen and in the adapter list.
  * Add the tests: pytest for ifutil and the dialogs, with coverage checked
    on every pull request.

 -- Keel Linux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:58:05 +0000

